WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.170
Speaker 1: I have not talked about White House
press secretary Jen Psaki press briefings

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:06.170
for a while.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:09.100
I've just been so busy with different elements
of the show.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.130
I haven't been watching them.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:11.960
I haven't been covering, but yesterday covering
them.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:17.289
But yesterday I did get an opportunity to
see kind of what was going on and something

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:20.140
the more things change, the more things stay
the same.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:23.660
Both Jen Psaki and Fox News reporter Peter
Doocy have had COVID.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:24.980
They're both back.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:30.160
And Peter Doocy is once again attempting these
takedowns of Jen Psaki and of Biden policy

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:31.160
on COVID.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:36.880
Now, there is no shortage of criticism of
the United States, both under Trump and under

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:42.180
Biden when it comes to COVID policy missteps
made under both without playing false equivalency.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:47.489
What Trump did is unconscionable in a completely
different way than the way that that Joe Biden

00:00:47.489 --> 00:00:50.899
has not been as good as he could have been
when it comes to COVID policy.

00:00:50.899 --> 00:00:58.450
But Peter Doocy tries to, in order to score
points against Jen Psaki, starts pushing anti-vax

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:03.680
talking points like vaccinated people are
getting it too, which of course, is a very

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:09.759
dangerous talking point in the abstract to
promote given the level of anti-vaccine sentiment

00:01:09.759 --> 00:01:14.679
in the United States, given the incredibly
significant protection that vaccines provide

00:01:14.679 --> 00:01:16.159
against hospitalization and death.

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:17.619
So let's just jump right in.

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:22.549
And I think this is an example of Jen Psaki
doing a pretty good job of refuting these

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:24.009
toxic talking points.

00:01:24.009 --> 00:01:31.969
Speaker 4: I understand the science says that
vaccines prevent death, but controversial

00:01:31.969 --> 00:01:34.649
vaccine still got COVID it triple backs.

00:01:34.649 --> 00:01:36.039
Still, God forbid.

00:01:36.039 --> 00:01:38.729
Why is the president still referring to this
as a pandemic?

00:01:38.729 --> 00:01:42.000
I'm vaccinated,
Speaker 1: and of course, the answer.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.060
Well, we'll see what Jen Psaki says.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:50.969
The answer is it's disproportionately the
unvaccinated who have to go to the hospital,

00:01:50.969 --> 00:01:58.149
who end up being intubated and who end up
dying, even though now most of the country,

00:01:58.149 --> 00:02:01.520
but by most, I don't mean 80 90 percent, but
60 something percent.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.920
Most of the country is vaccinated.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:06.789
It is still overwhelmingly the unvaccinated
that are getting really sick.

00:02:06.789 --> 00:02:07.789
That's what it means.

00:02:07.789 --> 00:02:08.869
OK, now let's listen to Jen Psaki.

00:02:08.869 --> 00:02:13.790
Speaker 5: Well, I think, Peter, there's a
significant difference between and you just

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:18.189
you just experienced this and not to expose
your public health experience, but I can speak

00:02:18.189 --> 00:02:20.060
to my own mind as well.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:21.829
I had been triple vaxxed.

00:02:21.829 --> 00:02:23.450
I had minor symptoms.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:26.890
There is a huge difference between that and
being unvaccinated.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:31.270
You are 17 times more likely to go to the
hospital if you're not vaccinated, 20 times

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:32.980
more likely to die.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:38.040
And those are significant serious statistics
if you suggest the impact for people who are

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.880
unvaccinated is far more dire than those who
are vaccinated.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:46.010
Speaker 4: Will the president update language
in some time to be more reflective of the

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:50.030
fact that people who are triple vaccinated
are catching and spreading COVID?

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:54.600
Speaker 5: I think people per president has
set, as have we a number of times, that there

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:55.910
will be breakthrough cases.

00:02:55.910 --> 00:03:01.060
There will be people who get COVID here at
different media organizations, at companies

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:05.040
around the world, around the country who have
been vaccinated.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:11.650
But there is a significant difference between
being hospitalized or dying and being vaccinated

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:12.650
with more mild symptoms.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:19.999
Speaker 1: So what you have to understand
is that Peter Doocy is there to try to goad

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:26.170
Jen Psaki into soundbites for the purposes
of later airing them on Fox News and showing

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.170
how great she did.

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:34.109
The questions are dumb, and they're bad questions
by design to ET because they're so stupid

00:03:34.109 --> 00:03:36.980
that the idea is fire up Jen Psaki.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:41.319
So she says something emotional or looks bad
in some way.

00:03:41.319 --> 00:03:46.739
He is not actually there to be a reporter
and to bring information to people.

00:03:46.739 --> 00:03:52.879
His argument essentially is seatbelt laws
haven't completely eliminated traffic deaths.

00:03:52.879 --> 00:03:57.989
And also, sometimes even when you're wearing
a seatbelt, you can still get hurt in a car

00:03:57.989 --> 00:03:58.989
accident.

00:03:58.989 --> 00:03:59.989
That's basically the argument.

00:03:59.989 --> 00:04:03.060
And if you said that to most people, they
would say that's a really stupid argument

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.900
against seatbelts, isn't it?

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:08.200
This is the most important of the three things
that that he kind of tries to pull.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.260
We'll look at a couple of others in a moment.

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:17.620
The unvaccinated in the U.S. are more likely
to test positive, so you still do get protection

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:20.820
against Macron from being triple vaccinated.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:26.370
But it is so contagious, and it's different
enough from what the vaccines target that

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:31.970
a lot of vaccinated people still ultimately
test positive, but they are significantly

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:36.169
less likely to end up in the hospital and
significantly less likely to die.

00:04:36.169 --> 00:04:40.470
It's sort of like a false equivalency where
he goes, Listen, unvaccinated people get this

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.110
and vaccinated people get this.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:43.110
So it's the same.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:46.660
Well, no, you have to actually look at the
numbers and see what it is that we're talking

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:47.660
about here and.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:52.599
The issue is they are coming to their conclusion
first, which is we don't like the vaccine,

00:04:52.599 --> 00:04:57.500
we want to talk about being against it, not
Doocy personally write his shtick as I got

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:00.750
it, but people are asking this question because
he's doing it for the audience.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:04.560
They start with, we don't want the vaccine
and then they work backwards from there.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.680
Then they also talked about COVID testing.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:07.970
I'll just show you a little bit of that.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:10.460
Speaker 4: I was home all last week, isolating.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:11.460
Welcome back.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:12.460
Thank you.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:14.729
I was isolating with COVID after a positive
test.

00:05:14.729 --> 00:05:20.020
Like a lot of people watching and a lot of
time in front of the TV, I heard the president

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.129
say, Did you watch
Speaker 5: Fox full time or other things?

00:05:22.129 --> 00:05:25.199
Speaker 4: I had exhausted the full catalog
of Guy.

00:05:25.199 --> 00:05:26.199
Very content.

00:05:26.199 --> 00:05:27.199
Speaker 5: Oh, OK.

00:05:27.199 --> 00:05:35.360
Speaker 4: Now obviously a lot of folks, but
I heard the president say Google COVID test

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:36.360
near me.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:42.130
So somebody isolating with COVID, I did that
and the appointments everywhere were completely

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:43.130
jammed.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:49.129
So why is it that you guys were so unprepared
for the need for testing after the holidays?

00:05:49.129 --> 00:05:54.030
Speaker 5: Well, Peter, I'm happy to see you
back and well, I would second say that there

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:59.479
has been a massive surge in cases, as you
know, and we're a part of in D.C. and New

00:05:59.479 --> 00:06:03.050
York, and there has been an unprecedented
in other parts of the country as well.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.820
There's been an unprecedented demand for tests.

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:09.860
So what we have done over the course of the
last few weeks even before.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:11.479
Speaker 1: So, you know, it's another gotcha.

00:06:11.479 --> 00:06:16.720
And it is absolutely true that testing is
a disaster in the United States.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:20.030
It's been a disaster for a long time.

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:30.319
And it's the the problem here is the continued
